<section image-layout="blank" id="B-uYnOS4oX" vertical-align="center" background-overlay="tint" background-overlay-intensity="0.38"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/Mg_38a9d0yi7UoPDDzimc.png" saved-media-id="yp22nbuc3imcvwu" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="celestial-copperplate" alt="Digitally illustrated copperplate celestial engraving of a brass telescope aimed across a vast deep-space field, precise ivory coordinate arcs widening across an abyssal-blue sky, cyan spectral traces and one restrained coral signal, a tiny generic ship silhouette low at the far right for scale, generous dark negative space on the left, no central explosion, no text or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1920,&quot;height&quot;:1088}"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="LPXLeEPBIr"><p role="eyebrow">No shore, no center</p><h1 font-size="52pt" style="padding-right: 34%;">Captain, reverse the telescope</h1><p font-size="lg" style="padding-right: 42%;"><b>Across distant galaxies, one clue repeats:</b> the universe is not debris racing from a blast point. Space itself has been stretching for about 13.8 billion years.</p><spacer size="24pt"></spacer><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="xs"><p font-size="sm">Our course follows three bearings · Expansion · Cooling · Evidence</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="54Yssyw4l1"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="Vp3q-YxvKg" vertical-align="center" colspan="34"><labels><label variant="outline">Log entry 01</label></labels><h2>The log begins hot and dense</h2><p font-size="18pt">The observable universe was once in an extremely hot, dense state. As space expanded, the universe cooled. Measurements place this history at about <b>13.8 billion years</b>.</p><p font-size="18pt">This is not a bomb’s launch time in a pre-existing void. The model describes the universe changing with time—not matter flying into an outer sea.</p><p role="caption">Source: <a href="https://science.nasa.gov/universe/overview/">NASA · Universe Overview</a></p></grid-item><grid-item id="926XgcszlN" padding="0" colspan="26"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/gvVGNyol0cPkAkVlmuh1A.png" saved-media-id="5iucvfr32zpvpk8" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="celestial-copperplate" alt="Copperplate scientific concept illustration of the uniformly hot dense early cosmos extending beyond every edge of the frame, nested unlabeled coordinate meshes and diffused cyan radiation traces with restrained oxidized-brass instrument arcs, abyssal blue field, no center, no outward blast, absolutely no text, numbers, symbols, tick labels, or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1440,&quot;height&quot;:1440}"><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="g8p68et-kQ" background-color="surface" padding="10pt 14pt"><p role="caption"><b>Concept illustration</b> · not observational data or a map of a blast.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="G7QUWdMXzz"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="jLYnoNS_fy"><h2>Stretch the chart, not the ships</h2><p font-size="18pt"><b>Chart test:</b> place three distant galaxies on a flexible coordinate grid, then enlarge the grid. Every pair separates; choosing A, B, or C as the viewpoint changes no result. None is the center.</p><freeform-block w="840" h="238"><shape preset="roundRect" y="8" w="382" h="202" fill="surface" stroke="palette-5" stroke-width="1"></shape><shape preset="roundRect" x="458" y="8" w="382" h="202" fill="surface" stroke="palette-5" stroke-width="1"></shape><box type="content" x="18" y="15" w="190"><p font-size="16pt"><b>Same marker identities</b></p></box><box type="content" x="476" y="15" w="190"><p font-size="16pt"><b>Coordinate grid enlarged</b></p></box><box type="content" x="45" y="42" w="1" h="148" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-5" style="opacity: 0.65;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="110" y="42" w="1" h="148" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-5" style="opacity: 0.65;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="175" y="42" w="1" h="148" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-5" style="opacity: 0.65;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="240" y="42" w="1" h="148" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-5" style="opacity: 0.65;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="305" y="42" w="1" h="148" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-5" style="opacity: 0.65;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="35" y="55" w="315" h="1" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-5" style="opacity: 0.65;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="35" y="100" w="315" h="1" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-5" style="opacity: 0.65;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="35" y="145" w="315" h="1" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-5" style="opacity: 0.65;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="35" y="190" w="315" h="1" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-5" style="opacity: 0.65;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="485" y="42" w="1" h="148" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-5" style="opacity: 0.65;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="580" y="42" w="1" h="148" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-5" style="opacity: 0.65;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="675" y="42" w="1" h="148" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-5" style="opacity: 0.65;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="770" y="42" w="1" h="148" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-5" style="opacity: 0.65;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="475" y="55" w="335" h="1" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-5" style="opacity: 0.65;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="475" y="120" w="335" h="1" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-5" style="opacity: 0.65;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="475" y="185" w="335" h="1" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-5" style="opacity: 0.65;"><p></p></box><shape preset="line" x="110" y="80" w="195" h="1" stroke="accent" stroke-width="2"></shape><shape preset="line" x="110" y="80" w="65" h="90" stroke="accent" stroke-width="2"></shape><shape preset="line" x="175" y="80" w="130" h="90" stroke="accent" stroke-width="2" flip-h="true"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="102" y="72" w="16" h="16" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="297" y="72" w="16" h="16" fill="palette-3" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="167" y="162" w="16" h="16" fill="accent" stroke-width="0"></shape><box type="content" x="86" y="87" w="24"><p font-size="16pt">A</p></box><box type="content" x="316" y="72" w="24"><p font-size="16pt">B</p></box><box type="content" x="184" y="167" w="24"><p font-size="16pt">C</p></box><shape preset="rightArrow" x="397" y="98" w="46" h="28" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="line" x="485" y="55" w="285" h="1" stroke="accent" stroke-width="2"></shape><shape preset="line" x="485" y="55" w="95" h="130" stroke="accent" stroke-width="2"></shape><shape preset="line" x="580" y="55" w="190" h="130" stroke="accent" stroke-width="2" flip-h="true"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="477" y="47" w="16" h="16" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="762" y="47" w="16" h="16" fill="palette-3" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="572" y="177" w="16" h="16" fill="accent" stroke-width="0"></shape><box type="content" x="468" y="65" w="24"><p font-size="16pt">A</p></box><box type="content" x="784" y="48" w="24"><p font-size="16pt">B</p></box><box type="content" x="594" y="178" w="24"><p font-size="16pt">C</p></box><box type="content" x="495" y="208" w="300"><p role="caption"><b>All three pairwise distances increase.</b></p></box></freeform-block><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="XQGBp8BldJ" colspan="30"><p font-size="16pt"><b>The grid</b> represents changing large-scale distances in space.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="BmtdeV67EM" colspan="30"><p font-size="16pt"><b>The markers</b> are not ships crossing a surrounding cosmic ocean.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption"><b>Scope:</b> this analogy describes widely separated, gravitationally unbound galaxies. Bound systems such as the Milky Way are not simply stretched by cosmic expansion.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="OQY-X6x27W"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="9EmSBbsNu8" padding-bottom="72pt"><h2>Expansion cools the cosmos</h2><p font-size="18pt"><b>As the universe expands, it cools—and what matter and light can do changes.</b> The stages below span radically different lengths of time.</p><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="0I-Vqk5vZL" cell-style="subtle" colspan="15"><h4>Expansion and cooling</h4><p font-size="16pt">The early universe begins hot and dense; growing distances accompany falling temperature.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="XnhrrnWAxk" cell-style="subtle" colspan="15"><h4>First minutes</h4><p font-size="16pt">Light atomic nuclei can persist as conditions cool.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ENWoT5Kfly" cell-style="subtle" colspan="15"><h4>≈380,000 years</h4><p font-size="16pt">Neutral atoms form; relic light begins traveling freely.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="58SM86s6Yo" cell-style="subtle" colspan="15"><h4>Hundreds of millions of years later</h4><p font-size="16pt">The first stars shine; galaxies develop over cosmic time.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption"><span text-color="palette-4">Schematic timeline · intervals are not proportional. Source: </span><a href="https://science.nasa.gov/universe/overview/">NASA · Universe Overview</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="Gppcu1tgFB"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="B5whB3WR2b"><h2>Redshift: light keeps the wake</h2><p font-size="18pt">During a galaxy’s light voyage, expanding space stretches the light’s wavelength toward longer, redder bands. This <b>cosmological redshift</b> is a stretched signal—not dye, smoke, or a red sail.</p><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="0PtIiZ-dCJ" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">At emission</p><h3>Shorter wavelength</h3><custom-code><style>.wake-short { height: 7.2em; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; } .wake-short svg { max-width: 100%; }</style><div class="wake-short"><svg viewBox="0 0 360 105" width="360" height="105" role="img" aria-label="A tightly spaced light wave"><line x1="10" y1="53" x2="350" y2="53" stroke="var(--body-color)" stroke-opacity=".25" stroke-dasharray="5 6"></line><path d="M10 53 C20 17 30 17 40 53 S60 89 70 53 S90 17 100 53 S120 89 130 53 S150 17 160 53 S180 89 190 53 S210 17 220 53 S240 89 250 53 S270 17 280 53 S300 89 310 53 S330 17 350 53" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent-color)" stroke-width="4"></path><circle cx="10" cy="53" r="6" fill="var(--accent-color)"></circle><circle cx="350" cy="53" r="6" fill="var(--accent-color)"></circle></svg></div></custom-code><p font-size="16pt">Successive crests begin close together.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="FpUkipYB8f" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">After cosmic travel</p><h3>Longer wavelength</h3><custom-code><style>.wake-long { height: 7.2em; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; } .wake-long svg { max-width: 100%; }</style><div class="wake-long"><svg viewBox="0 0 360 105" width="360" height="105" role="img" aria-label="A stretched light wave with wider crest spacing"><line x1="10" y1="53" x2="350" y2="53" stroke="var(--body-color)" stroke-opacity=".25" stroke-dasharray="5 6"></line><path d="M10 53 C38 12 66 12 94 53 S150 94 178 53 S234 12 262 53 S318 94 350 53" fill="none" stroke="var(--palette-3, var(--accent-color))" stroke-width="4"></path><circle cx="10" cy="53" r="6" fill="var(--accent-color)"></circle><circle cx="350" cy="53" r="6" fill="var(--palette-3, var(--accent-color))"></circle></svg></div></custom-code><p font-size="16pt">Expansion increases the crest-to-crest distance.</p></grid-item></grid><p font-size="16pt">Across distant galaxies, this pattern is evidence that space expanded while their light traveled.</p><p role="caption">Source: <a href="https://science.nasa.gov/mission/hubble/science/science-behind-the-discoveries/hubble-big-bang/">NASA/Hubble · Big Bang evidence</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="dgwqTqMjen" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="KjI3GeAm2K" vertical-align="center" colspan="25"><p role="eyebrow">Evidence bearing 02</p><h2>Relic light on every horizon</h2><display size="md" font-size="44pt">≈380,000 years</display><p font-size="18pt">The universe became transparent enough for light to travel freely; expansion has since cooled that relic light into microwaves.</p><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="xs"><h4>Cosmic microwave background</h4><p font-size="18pt">We detect it across the sky—not from one central blast port.</p><p font-size="13pt">Source: <a href="https://science.nasa.gov/universe/overview/">NASA · Universe Overview</a></p></grid-item><grid-item id="5_L16S4Eom" vertical-align="center" colspan="35"><labels><label variant="outline">Conceptual all-sky direction map</label></labels><h3>Relic light arrives from around us</h3><freeform-block w="500" h="292"><shape preset="roundRect" w="500" h="292" fill="surface" stroke="palette-5" stroke-width="1"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="40" y="42" w="420" h="196" fill="surface" stroke="accent" stroke-width="2"></shape><shape preset="line" x="72" y="78" w="178" h="70" stroke="palette-5" stroke-width="1"></shape><shape preset="line" x="250" y="78" w="178" h="70" stroke="palette-5" stroke-width="1" flip-h="true"></shape><shape preset="line" x="48" y="145" w="202" h="4" stroke="palette-5" stroke-width="1"></shape><shape preset="line" x="250" y="145" w="202" h="4" stroke="palette-5" stroke-width="1"></shape><shape preset="line" x="82" y="148" w="168" h="66" stroke="palette-5" stroke-width="1" flip-h="true"></shape><shape preset="line" x="250" y="148" w="168" h="66" stroke="palette-5" stroke-width="1"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="82" y="72" w="34" h="24" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="144" y="102" w="45" h="28" fill="accent" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="215" y="65" w="30" h="22" fill="palette-3" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="285" y="92" w="54" h="30" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="365" y="66" w="38" h="26" fill="accent" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="105" y="160" w="52" h="30" fill="palette-3" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="181" y="184" w="40" h="24" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="296" y="166" w="38" h="26" fill="accent" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="370" y="177" w="48" h="27" fill="palette-3" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="236" y="134" w="28" h="28" fill="palette-4" stroke="accent" stroke-width="2"></shape><box type="content" x="195" y="164" w="110"><p font-size="16pt" align="center"><b>Observer</b></p></box><box type="content" x="55" y="248" w="390"><p font-size="16pt" align="center">Centered in this sky view—not at the center of the universe.</p></box></freeform-block><p font-size="13pt">The oval maps arrival directions, not a physical shell. Mottling is schematic, not measured CMB temperature data.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="rgYe7pz2V3" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="c5ebnafYzH"><h2>A good chart marks its limits</h2><p font-size="18pt"><b>The model charts evolution, not every origin question.</b> Honest navigators separate the evidence-supported route from what remains beyond the chart.</p><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="ADjs_arDBY" border="2.6666666666666665px dashed palette-5" colspan="18"><labels><label variant="outline">Boundary marked</label></labels><h3>Before the earliest described phase</h3><p font-size="17pt">What preceded it remains uncertain. The model supplies no known launch point, outer void, or certain first cause.</p><p><b>The limit is part of the chart.</b></p></grid-item><grid-item id="xStgClGF_n" background-color="surface" colspan="42"><labels><label variant="solid">Evidence-supported route</label></labels><h3>Development of the observable universe</h3><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="c2BN5a6hlO" colspan="15"><h4>Hot, dense phase</h4><p font-size="16pt">The model begins with early conditions.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="PiX6Ma_hTH" colspan="15"><h4>Nuclei</h4><p font-size="16pt">Cooling allows light nuclei to persist.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="03FwafCcaE" colspan="15"><h4>Atoms + free light</h4><p font-size="16pt">At about 380,000 years.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="o5Vgx67VBB" colspan="15"><h4>Stars + galaxies</h4><p font-size="16pt">Structure develops later.</p></grid-item></grid><p font-size="16pt"><b>No privileged center or navigable edge is required.</b></p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Source: <a href="https://science.nasa.gov/universe/overview/">NASA · Universe Overview</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="-ZBEtibu6V" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="XAR-suzOL4"><p role="eyebrow">Final position</p><h2>Three bearings, one cosmic history</h2><p font-size="18pt"><b>Keep the relationships together.</b> Expansion changes conditions; two different observations let us test that course.</p><freeform-block w="840" h="220"><shape preset="rightArrow" x="292" y="50" w="256" h="28" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="line" x="250" y="98" w="45" h="38" stroke="accent" stroke-width="2"></shape><shape preset="line" x="545" y="98" w="45" h="38" stroke="accent" stroke-width="2" flip-h="true"></shape><box type="content" y="10" w="250" h="96" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 14pt 18pt;"><h3>Expansion</h3><p font-size="16pt">On large scales, distances between unbound galaxies grow.</p></box><box type="content" x="590" y="10" w="250" h="96" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 14pt 18pt;"><h3>Cooling</h3><p font-size="16pt">Changing conditions allow nuclei, atoms, stars, and galaxies.</p></box><box type="content" x="310" y="14" w="220"><p role="caption" align="center"><b>EXPANSION CHANGES TEMPERATURE</b></p></box><box type="content" x="120" y="114" w="180"><p role="caption" align="center">Redshift checks expansion</p></box><box type="content" x="540" y="114" w="180"><p role="caption" align="center">Relic light records cooling</p></box><box type="content" x="295" y="138" w="250" h="72" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="accent" style="padding: 12pt 18pt;"><h3 align="center">Evidence</h3><p font-size="16pt" align="center">Two bearings test the same voyage.</p></box></freeform-block><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="85X9VyONww" background-color="accent" padding="14pt 18pt"><p font-size="18pt"><b>If asked where it happened:</b> not at one cosmic port. On large scales, the history belongs to the universe itself.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>